Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.810
speaking of Elizabeth Warren yesterday I told
you that Elizabeth Warren had taken a one

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:11.610
point lead in the New Hampshire primary over
Biden and a two point lead in New Hampshire

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:12.630
over Bernie.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:18.430
Now since then, we have had another New Hampshire
poll which shows Bernie ahead and we also

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:26.340
have a new national economist poll, which
has Elizabeth Warren tied with Joe Biden Nationally

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.230
26 to 26 this is not a single state.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:30.230
Okay.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:35.470
This is national polling other than a single
Monmouth poll in mid August, Joe Biden has

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:42.550
led every poll nationally dating all the way
back to before he even announced he was running

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:48.070
and we now have tonight a Democratic primary
debate where Elizabeth Warren is at least

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:55.830
in one poll, not trying to catch Joe Biden
but co front runner with Joe Biden at 26 26

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.240
so let's look at this one pole.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.440
And remember it's just one pole, but this
is still very, very notable.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.930
Also notable is that in this poll, Bernie
Sanders is all the way down to 16% which I

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:09.960
actually do find difficult to believe.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.850
So it's always important to consider one poll.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:12.850
No more than that.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:14.770
It is just one data point.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:19.370
Unless there has been a significant real shift
away from Bernie towards Warren.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:24.390
It's difficult to imagine that both Bernie
and Warren are each 10 points ahead of Bernie,

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:31.060
but this is one poll, so now that we've seen
this, what you need to do is nothing different.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:34.070
What I mean is it's the same situation as
always.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:38.680
You need to stay engaged, you need to go vote
when your state votes, no matter what the

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.090
polls say.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:45.130
But this is very interesting in terms of the
dynamics for tonight's debate, which for me

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:48.300
has become a lot more interesting in light
of these recent polling changes.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:55.250
Will the tone and the feel of tonight's debate
be different because Warren is no longer,

00:01:55.250 --> 00:02:00.460
at least in this poll, trying to come from
behind Biden and make her case, but rather

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:01.990
a co front runner.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:05.229
If you are Biden, are you panicking?

00:02:05.229 --> 00:02:06.229
Maybe not.

00:02:06.229 --> 00:02:10.869
It's unclear how much Joe Biden actually wants
to be president, but presuming that he really

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:15.330
does want to be president of the United States,
if you are Joe Biden, you have to be worried

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:17.040
about Elizabeth Warren's momentum.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.980
I got some emails yesterday in light of this
new poll saying, Hey, David Biden's should

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.320
step down.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:25.750
I find this a little bit silly.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:30.010
Rarely would anyone who is leading, even if
it's tied for the lead.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:35.670
Step aside, unless the argument about momentum
is so overwhelming and Biden really doesn't

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:41.430
want to be president of the United States,
I don't see Biden stepping down anytime soon,

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:45.440
but now there is a real fight and the questions
of speaking time in tonight's debate will

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:46.930
be immediate questions.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:53.850
We tend to see those who are leading get disproportionately
more speaking time and while in one sense

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:54.900
that's completely unfair.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.209
In another sense, it's completely expected.

00:02:57.209 --> 00:03:01.130
Once you understand the corporate nature of
these debates on the major networks, will

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:05.880
speaking time be impacted by the fact that
at least in this poll, Elizabeth Warren is

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.800
a co front runner with Joe Biden.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:08.800
We

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:09.800
will have to see.

